.debug_loclists: contribution length checked against the whole section, not the bytes left after its offset (heap over-read, sibling of #336)
 #342
￼
New issue
￼
This is the .debug_loclists version of #336.
_dwarf_internal_read_loclists_header()
(src/lib/libdwarf/dwarf_loclists.c:395-396 on master
71f0401) checks a contribution's length against the size
of the whole section and ignores the contribution's offset:

    if (arealen > sectionlength ||
        (arealen+offset_size+exten_size) > sectionlength) {

A contribution that does not start at offset 0 can
therefore declare an end past the end of the section.
The list reader then reads past the section buffer. Here
is a 26-byte section with two contributions. The second
starts at 0x0d and declares unit_length 17, so it ends
at 0x22. Its single list entry is DW_LLE_base_address,
which reads an 8-byte operand:


